From: armourpiercer1 <gtx21@mails.tsinghua.edu.cn>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:49:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] NATIVE-BASH-PRESERVATION: the governed bash is the host's own
 definition over a Member-bound PTY
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Alpha.5's invariant (ADR D2, A5-NATIVE-01/02, A5-BOUNDARY-01) is that a native
tool's EXECUTION BACKEND may be replaced, never the tool. The governed Preview
shipped three Team-authored `bash` definitions instead (PD-12's confined-bash,
PD-13's confined-terminal, and the tool plane's `team_bash`); the plane's row is
what the Alpha.6 junction executed, leaving 0 guard facts in the realm sink.

The model-visible `bash` is now the PINNED @deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-bash-persistent
definition, mounted by route C on the Member's isolated scope. `execute` alone is
wrapped: the Team admission edge (the plane's own lane decision + paAdmit, i.e.
Alpha.4 allow/ask/deny and Alpha.6 approval with one-shot consumption) runs in
FRONT of the native call, and nothing else about the definition changes — name,
description, parameter schema, output/render and presentCall are the host's own
values.

The execution backend is a new governed persistent-PTY `terminals` face
(team-services/terminal-pty.ts). It registers no tool and re-implements no PTY
mechanics: it mounts the pinned terminal-bash backend through that module's own
`apply` over a ctx facade and wraps the pinned TerminalSessionService on a
nested isolate. The Member ceiling enters exactly where the pinned backend
already reads it — `sandboxPolicy.resolve({session})` is narrowed to the
Member's own write root, `danger-full-access` is clamped, `read-only` is never
lifted, and a cwd outside every declared root degrades to read-only instead of
guessing a root. Identity is EXACT: the owner's session id must equal the one
Member session the face was installed for (no prefix, no includes), and a face
with no bound session refuses every spawn before a PTY exists. Every session
records the policy revision it opened under; a send under a superseded revision
kills the session with a typed refusal, so no stale permission domain survives.
Disposal kills every session the face opened. Every failure is a typed refusal
(PTY_OWNER_UNBOUND / PTY_OWNER_MISMATCH / PTY_CEILING_STALE / PTY_POLICY_STALE /
PTY_WRITE_ROOT_UNAVAILABLE / ENFORCEMENT_UNAVAILABLE / PTY_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE) —
never the inherited host PTY.

Wiring: the shipped composition (host.ts) declares `nativeBashPty`, so the
product's realm carries the PTY face; install.ts mounts it for a `mode: 'pty'`
terminal spec and requires the sandbox + base subprocess seams (refusing, not
downgrading); a5sf-realm-row gains `nativeBashPtySpecOf`, which outranks the
PD-12/PD-13 shadows only for a face carrying the `governedPty` marker; the plane
skips its own shell row when `plane.nativeBashAdopted` is set, so no second Team
shell competes with the native name, and exposes `admitNative`/`settleNative`,
published per runtime Agent by agent-bindings.

Retirement is additive: the PD-12/PD-13 modules, PD-13's face and the plane's
row stay (with their specs and their own suites) and carry a RETIRED FROM THE
PRODUCT PATH banner. The docs-lane paragraph for the release notes is supplied in
the lane evidence README; RELEASE-NOTES-0.1.6.md is untouched.

Honest bounds: this path enforces what the OS profile enforces — it adds no read
allowlist, and the evidence README states that. THE REAL-HOST ACCEPTANCE IS NOT
MET in this lane: the only live governed-realm harness measures the ungoverned
PTY, and the C1 kit's team row declares no `a5sfGovernedRealm`, so neither
exercises the new face. Two fresh-DSH_HOME runs remain outstanding; the measured
cause and the exact next step are in dev/agent-workflow/evidence/
native-bash-preservation/README.md, together with the 13/13 host-free contract
suite that does not substitute for them.

